an70/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/evan70","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/responsive-sk/resp-native-boot-DDD/commits/190877338c454ae276636aafe26081cd0edcce8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-06T09:14:49Z","email":"ivan.paldan@yandex.com","name":"Ivan Paldan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-06T09:14:49Z","email":"ivan.paldan@yandex.com","name":"Ivan Paldan"},"message":"Fix AuthMiddleware API vs Web response handling\n\nProblems solved:\n- API requests were receiving HTML redirects instead of JSON errors\n- Web requests were not properly differentiated from API requests\n- Inconsistent response formats for different request types\n\nSolution implemented:\n- API request detection via path prefix and Accept header\n- JSON error responses for API authentication/authorization failures\n- HTML redirects for web authentication/authorization failures\n- Proper HTTP status codes (401/403 for API, 302 for web)\n\nResponse types:\n- API: JSON with error/message fields, appropriate status codes\n- Web: HTTP redirects to login/authorized pages\n- Accept header detection for API requests\n- Path-based detection for API endpoints\n\nBenefits:\n- RESTful API behavior with proper error responses\n- Better developer experience for API consumers\n- Consistent web application behavior with redirects\n- Proper HTTP status code usage","tree":{"sha":"4b86eeede1cabaab35d47e49921557e8d95b62bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/responsive-sk/resp-native-boot-DDD/git/trees/4b86eeede1cabaab35d47e49921557e8d95b62bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/responsive-sk/resp-native-boot-DDD/git/commits/190877338c454ae276636aafe26081cd0edcce8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67433?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evan70/events{/privacy}","fo