s/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/faa8fdd1fc761af47df3349259c64d86a4dc7397/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:57:33Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:57:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(engine): add opt-in Codemode plugin (#1067)\n\n* feat(engine): add opt-in Codemode plugin\n\n* fix(engine): trim Codemode runtime distribution\n\n* fix(engine): share runtime chunks and use compact schema validation\n\n* feat(engine): expose enabled MCP tools to Codemode by default\n\n* fix(engine): isolate presentation tool objects from policy wrappers\n\n* feat(canvas): opt-in Codemode integration, chat details and tracing (#1069)\n\n* build(engine): revert tsup splitting/minify from Codemode branch\n\nRestore the master tsup config (no splitting, no minify, single es2022\ntarget). The distribution change affects every engine consumer and is not\nrequired by Codemode: both ESM and CJS barrels load and run the Codemode\nworker without it. Drop the matching Distribution note from the engine\narchitecture knowledge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* feat(canvas): opt-in Codemode with read-only Canvas tool allowlist\n\nRegister the agent-codemode experimental flag (default off). When it is\non, the Canvas engine plugin list installs the Engine Codemode plugin and\nauthorizes only read/search/list/layout Canvas tools for scripts; Canvas\nwrites, agent messaging, terminals and plugin actions stay direct-only.\nEnabled MCP tools follow the Engine default and keep the existing Ask\nmode beforeToolCall gate per nested call.\n\nRecord the boundary in Canvas security posture and update the Codemode\nspec status.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* feat(canvas): show Codemode script calls in chat and nest them in traces\n\nRender a Codemode tool row from its persisted result: the summary counts\nscript calls and failures, and the expanded details list grouped nested\ncalls (status, duration, policy interception, errors) before the script\noutput and the folded script source. Completed and reloaded turns use the\nsame data, so no new IPC or persistence field is needed.\n\nTool trace events now carry parentToolCallId for script calls; Langfuse\nnests them under the outer tool span and the DevTools timeline marks them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* fix(engine): keep MCP App tools out of Codemode scripts\n\nRegister MCP tools that declare a ui:// resource with codemode: false, as\nthe Codemode spec requires: a script call would return data without the\nhost''s App instance, UI card or confirmation flow. Plain MCP tools stay\nscript-eligible by default, and false still overrides a host allowlist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* fix(canvas): show the folded Codemode script before its calls\n\nPut the script source first in the Codemode details, folded by default,\nso it is reachable without scrolling while the nested call list stays\nvisible in the first view.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(engine): clarify Codemode tool invocation in discovery and errors\n\n* build(canvas): allow 243 MiB arm64 app budget\n\n* build(canvas): set arm64 app size gate to 256 MiB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc1a0a75eed2a4051f2dd5e9e0e8c1025c955f71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/cc1a0a75eed2a4051f2dd5e9e0e8c1025c955f71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/faa8fdd1fc761af47df3349259c64d86a4dc7397","verification":{"payload":"tree cc1a0a75eed2a4051f2dd5e9e0e8c1025c955f71\nparent 7777409c7e7c7bc9c84ccc6e118f0e9b880e5223\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790949453 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790949453 +0800\n\nfeat(engine): add opt-in Codemode plugin (#1067)\n\n* feat(engine): add opt-in Codemode plugin\n\n* fix(engine): trim Codemode runtime distribution\n\n* fix(engine): share runtime chunks and use compact schema validation\n\n* feat(engine): expose enabled MCP tools to Codemode by default\n\n* fix(engine): isolate presentation tool objects from policy wrappers\n\n* feat(canvas): opt-in Codemode integration, chat details and tracing (#1069)\n\n* build(engine): revert tsup splitting/minify from Codemode branch\n\nRestore the master tsup config (no splitting, no minify, single es2022\ntarget). The distribution change affects every engine consumer and is not\nrequired by Codemode: both ESM and CJS barrels load and run the Codemode\nworker without it. Drop the matching Distribution note from the engine\narchitecture knowledge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* feat(canvas): opt-in Codemode with read-only Canvas tool allowlist\n\nRegister the agent-codemode experimental flag (default off). When it is\non, the Canvas engine plugin list installs the Engine Codemode plugin and\nauthorizes only read/search/list/layout Canvas tools for scripts; Canvas\nwrites, agent messaging, terminals and plugin actions stay direct-only.\nEnabled MCP tools follow the Engine default and keep the existing Ask\nmode beforeToolCall gate per nested call.\n\nRecord the boundary in Canvas security posture and update the Codemode\nspec status.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* feat(canvas): show Codemode script calls in chat and nest them in traces\n\nRender a Codemode tool row from its persisted result: the summary counts\nscript calls and failures, and the expanded details list grouped nested\ncalls (status, duration, policy interception, errors) before the script\noutput and the folded script source. Completed and reloaded turns use the\nsame data, so no new IPC or persistence field is needed.\n\nTool trace events now carry parentToolCallId for script calls; Langfuse\nnests them under the outer tool span and the DevTools timeline marks them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* fix(engine): keep MCP App tools out of Codemode scripts\n\nRegister MCP tools that declare a ui:// resource with codemode: false, as\nthe Codemode spec requires: a script call would return data without the\nhost''s App instance, UI card or confirmation flow. Plain MCP tools stay\nscript-eligible by default, and false still overrides a host allowlist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n* fix(canvas): show the folded Codemode script before its calls\n\nPut the script source first in the Codemode details, folded by default,\nso it is reachable without scrolling while the nested call list stays\nvisible in the first view.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DQi3uq6rgAboVg3KQKXoJV\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(engine): clarify Codemode tool invocation in discovery and errors\n\n* build(canvas): allow 243 MiB arm64 app budget\n\n* build(canvas): set arm64 app size gate to 256 MiB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv7hNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsiIQABeGQ+YqoeGCCGp6N18dOFvN\nSJ4kbSU6MWf9CYKrvrF8xPsw1b7S1AjNxqcooND6XOmw4gtxTa0yK245VeT2nbcH\n4u4UEmy4fY9F0ZIkMz2hghhAA9g5ZCoyDpsPp3E7h9Ip59wPjr1nwL+me5V+R7wJ\nIlERh3PRB3+TVKKp3IkeNDtUhCVL0GxtP+dQfSLeID3buS95VkH9/zV7IyOlb9lT\nvu47jmuxrSFWPUWeLqlq3QX3WZT4gZrBjKAQniN2ZFj2XFvIZ/RbwlY7ASwXd6zX\nYOqnwOrknnEUNiZ9NfzqZEpeq/1+9O+6HdGGezZn4SQ7B9FvKHekv/7N0MNHIWaS\njjfFrZUW3pWP5JbOoCF4vFbMVYteZpsaJEELOPADssV3BQuy5pcgmCBNorcV3Z6l\nMBiK5CPh7SV1nlkUwqPLwYgS+ojiP/tZRmkpC3nE4vRcV4v9gftltunETkp3g3Ul\nLof4avbuQfWaOUfkPiG9glfx/6Vs43q7x1FRfi7+iuQgG1yOJpFU1r3KJofesMUK\n3lndDMSdUodaPeNlVoU9OtTuvi7dq5ZL0HXp+Nx6zM0jgYCBg3z6JrxHcTuiBHQP\n9KLDEICCNxQ9Ei8yyHTiZUXTlhZhiOTdIXwQQpOGCGhSjDEtZI4tVOkKqVZcVm9m\ngrEVkkddJUqXWmL30aOa\n=OwoY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T13:57:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login