eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/bc536153837132148eda238ec615d2dc9108a218/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:58:34Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:58:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(canvas): open MCP App nodes and expose their content to the Agent (#1065)\n\n* docs(canvas): record MCP Apps direction for external plugin nodes\n\nKeep the software-lego model (plugin node types, multiple instances,\nread/write/action) and prefer MCP Apps over MF2 as the UI transport for\nnew external plugins. Define a Pulse `node` entrypoint under `pulse/ui`,\nopen nodes with `{}` like OpenAI global/thread entrypoints, carry\ninstance identity in host context, and map OpenAI global/thread/file\nentrypoints and deep links for compatibility. Direction only; no code\nchanges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* docs(canvas): separate host binding from plugin state for MCP Apps nodes\n\nDrop the MF2-era payload contract from the MCP Apps direction: the host\nowns only the instance binding (the sole target of write), stores an\nopaque UI snapshot like Apps SDK widgetState without interpreting it,\nand leaves business data to the plugin server behind read/action tools.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* docs(canvas): record initial decisions for MCP Apps plugin nodes\n\nUse OpenAI''s bits-and-bolts example as the first compatibility slice,\nkeep every node view live for now, and set the permission defaults for\nuser-triggered calls, Agent actions, and view CSP.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* feat(canvas): open MCP App entrypoints as canvas nodes\n\nPlace MCP Apps on the canvas from static entrypoints, per the\nsoftware-lego MCP Apps direction.\n\n- engine: parse `_meta[\"<ns>/ui\"].entrypoints` and tool titles for MCP\n  App tools; add MCPAppsManager.listToolApps()\n- main: list entrypoints (Pulse `node` > OpenAI `global` > `thread`,\n  duplicate thread tabs dropped) and open one with `{}` without the\n  in-app approval; only declared entrypoint tools are callable\n- plugin node `mcp-apps/mcp-app` whose payload is the host-owned binding;\n  main `read` points the Agent at the server''s MCP tools\n- McpAppFrame `embedded` mode renders the iframe in place inside the node\n  so canvas zoom, clipping and stacking apply; host context carries\n  `pulse/node`\n- right-click create menu lists MCP Apps; popovers re-clamp when they\n  grow after opening\n- docs: knowledge facts and roadmap implementation status\n\nVerified in the real app with OpenAI''s bits-and-bolts example via\nmcp.json: create, two instances, restore after restart.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* fix(canvas): expose MCP App node context and prioritize references\n\n* perf(canvas): lazy load MCP App sandbox and context handlers\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"47e0f6a4f5ab5452fb7c8177c4daaef7df9238cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/47e0f6a4f5ab5452fb7c8177c4daaef7df9238cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/bc536153837132148eda238ec615d2dc9108a218","verification":{"payload":"tree 47e0f6a4f5ab5452fb7c8177c4daaef7df9238cf\nparent 52d88bf12cb549a6589d5a02c31e96bccd573fe0\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790769514 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790769514 +0800\n\nfeat(canvas): open MCP App nodes and expose their content to the Agent (#1065)\n\n* docs(canvas): record MCP Apps direction for external plugin nodes\n\nKeep the software-lego model (plugin node types, multiple instances,\nread/write/action) and prefer MCP Apps over MF2 as the UI transport for\nnew external plugins. Define a Pulse `node` entrypoint under `pulse/ui`,\nopen nodes with `{}` like OpenAI global/thread entrypoints, carry\ninstance identity in host context, and map OpenAI global/thread/file\nentrypoints and deep links for compatibility. Direction only; no code\nchanges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* docs(canvas): separate host binding from plugin state for MCP Apps nodes\n\nDrop the MF2-era payload contract from the MCP Apps direction: the host\nowns only the instance binding (the sole target of write), stores an\nopaque UI snapshot like Apps SDK widgetState without interpreting it,\nand leaves business data to the plugin server behind read/action tools.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* docs(canvas): record initial decisions for MCP Apps plugin nodes\n\nUse OpenAI''s bits-and-bolts example as the first compatibility slice,\nkeep every node view live for now, and set the permission defaults for\nuser-triggered calls, Agent actions, and view CSP.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* feat(canvas): open MCP App entrypoints as canvas nodes\n\nPlace MCP Apps on the canvas from static entrypoints, per the\nsoftware-lego MCP Apps direction.\n\n- engine: parse `_meta[\"<ns>/ui\"].entrypoints` and tool titles for MCP\n  App tools; add MCPAppsManager.listToolApps()\n- main: list entrypoints (Pulse `node` > OpenAI `global` > `thread`,\n  duplicate thread tabs dropped) and open one with `{}` without the\n  in-app approval; only declared entrypoint tools are callable\n- plugin node `mcp-apps/mcp-app` whose payload is the host-owned binding;\n  main `read` points the Agent at the server''s MCP tools\n- McpAppFrame `embedded` mode renders the iframe in place inside the node\n  so canvas zoom, clipping and stacking apply; host context carries\n  `pulse/node`\n- right-click create menu lists MCP Apps; popovers re-clamp when they\n  grow after opening\n- docs: knowledge facts and roadmap implementation status\n\nVerified in the real app with OpenAI''s bits-and-bolts example via\nmcp.json: create, two instances, restore after restart.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LKHJmgLmGrmSoDi3f4WnL\n\n* fix(canvas): expose MCP App node context and prioritize references\n\n* perf(canvas): lazy load MCP App sandbox and context handlers\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPlqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALkYQAAOGfVhLEg2tPANe6SIJnkil\nVFXIHznFYSe06rQui46Lh6OOktMXYfStkFt2TuBAEY6PkKd6deFZAUsvDbq/ctV7\nQKosQiS+10CkpV6SY2VxfhLA8eo3ZsnpLqOEXPWSbmEwWb8JWH487TYfD5doqoqv\nIDqP/GvOX/FTi06m9lAOCj231wN3o3K/3NrZKjgG8Ee7JpDtAyAzFD5bZGmlB9DR\nhjGo5YmnOCVGl2C9aJ6Knlem6DA0nDGiUQ5BhtOw8NwyFLswIMiuEjFpfUFr41AV\nkH9c6jfGCmlCb9e/AOneSyH9NHXvmolQz5uqYqbog3SCMzEtN0Mvaj4qQAISwxXk\naGXIet3Rtm66db3NJfFHcHlKDG3ndrOe1yz2KDtcDr8g5JaoE6mtE2eaBITYHL9L\n561fBjNn8tKxq9Zpq8HQi5QliTHrbARAQ5Tf9/VSQoav7Vk9T7AqcVNL4Ujyn5vY\njKRZI1F8g4GDUASS5iv8Cv8/815+EPxOJe47Rc7I0u+UF/FYmHpOZv621JiN2KC2\no7EIZBAdinmrlU0HuhFgAJiQLxuuWzcuZ1Jao4AhwEHKoW8GipGUqSb6cKJV3Ttq\nb