s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/c67c0c472a8632c33e9a3305821dde5bcfe24699","node_id":"C_kwDORBlpqtoAKGM2N2MwYzQ3MmE4NjMyYzMzZTlhMzMwNTgyMWRkZTViY2ZlMjQ2OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/fd76a9e7a0ae6996d665bf3760c07b4d3dbff29d","sha":"fd76a9e7a0ae6996d665bf3760c07b4d3dbff29d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/fd76a9e7a0ae6996d665bf3760c07b4d3dbff29d"}],"sha":"c67c0c472a8632c33e9a3305821dde5bcfe24699","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/c67c0c472a8632c33e9a3305821dde5bcfe24699"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47221942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/fd76a9e7a0ae6996d665bf3760c07b4d3dbff29d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T09:30:28Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T09:30:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Claude/compassionate hawking tkru9u (#1059)\n\n* fix(canvas): make @ mention popup responsive and align fork button\n\nThe @ popup lagged on every keystroke: the main process re-read and\ndecoded every stored session to match titles, the renderer held all\nlocal rows until that search answered (clearing the list and flashing a\nspinner each keystroke), and role/plugin lookups ran sequentially and\nblocked on IPC once their 5s caches expired.\n\n- Cache the session-title index in main for 10s with in-flight dedupe.\n- Paint local matches immediately; append session hits when they land,\n  and keep current rows visible while refining an open popup.\n- Load roles and plugins concurrently; serve their expired caches\n  stale-while-revalidate.\n- Style the message fork button like its copy/regenerate siblings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n* perf(canvas): search @ session titles from list metadata only\n\nThe @-mention session search decoded every stored session with all its\nmessages just to read the first user message. Match against the list\nmetadata the session rail already reads instead (SQLite conversation\nheaders / the legacy metadata index): stored preview, user title and\nworkspace name. No message bodies are loaded, so the interim 10s index\ncache is dropped and new sessions are searchable immediately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n* perf(canvas): debounce find-in-canvas and cache its scan inputs\n\nEvery keystroke in the Ctrl+F bar set `query` on the canvas controller,\nre-rendering the whole canvas, re-sorting all nodes, re-stripping every\nfile node''s HTML, and re-running the note-editor activation/highlight\npass for all content matches.\n\n- SearchBar keeps a local draft and commits it after 150ms of quiet;\n  Enter/arrows/nav buttons commit a pending draft immediately.\n- A new query or case mode resets the cursor to its first match.\n- Geometry ordering is memoized on nodes; stripped file text is cached\n  per data object.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n* fix(canvas): restore the default-browser toggle in Settings → Experimental\n\n`grandfathered` exposure hid the toggle from anyone who had not already\nenabled it, and turning it off made it un-re-enableable: the list kept\nshowing the switch but `experimental:set` then rejected it as \"not\nconfigurable\". Make it a regular experimental opt-in again (still off by\ndefault, still labelled not recommended).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e1a9f83ae2aca8f30ac788a6078e9ffa42839c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/1e1a9f83ae2aca8f30ac788a6078e9ffa42839c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/fd76a9e7a0ae6996d665bf3760c07b4d3dbff29d","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e1a9f83ae2aca8f30ac788a6078e9ffa42839c0\nparent 0f69fde7a0ec7046ee04e1e937efd97321099e04\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790587828 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790587828 +0800\n\nClaude/compassionate hawking tkru9u (#1059)\n\n* fix(canvas): make @ mention popup responsive and align fork button\n\nThe @ popup lagged on every keystroke: the main process re-read and\ndecoded every stored session to match titles, the renderer held all\nlocal rows until that search answered (clearing the list and flashing a\nspinner each keystroke), and role/plugin lookups ran sequentially and\nblocked on IPC once their 5s caches expired.\n\n- Cache the session-title index in main for 10s with in-flight dedupe.\n- Paint local matches immediately; append session hits when they land,\n  and keep current rows visible while refining an open popup.\n- Load roles and plugins concurrently; serve their expired caches\n  stale-while-revalidate.\n- Style the message fork button like its copy/regenerate siblings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n* perf(canvas): search @ session titles from list metadata only\n\nThe @-mention session search decoded every stored session with all its\nmessages just to read the first user message. Match against the list\nmetadata the session rail already reads instead (SQLite conversation\nheaders / the legacy metadata index): stored preview, user title and\nworkspace name. No message bodies are loaded, so the interim 10s index\ncache is dropped and new sessions are searchable immediately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n* perf(canvas): debounce find-in-canvas and cache its scan inputs\n\nEvery keystroke in the Ctrl+F bar set `query` on the canvas controller,\nre-rendering the whole canvas, re-sorting all nodes, re-stripping every\nfile node''s HTML, and re-running the note-editor activation/highlight\npass for all content matches.\n\n- SearchBar keeps a local draft and commits it after 150ms of quiet;\n  Enter/arrows/nav buttons commit a pending draft immediately.\n- A new query or case mode resets the cursor to its first match.\n- Geometry ordering is memoized on nodes; stripped file text is cached\n  per data object.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n* fix(canvas): restore the default-browser toggle in Settings → Experimental\n\n`grandfathered` exposure hid the toggle from anyone who had not already\nenabled it, and turning it off made it un-re-enableable: the list kept\nshowing the switch but `experimental:set` then rejected it as \"not\nconfigurable\". Make it a regular experimental opt-in again (still off by\ndefault, still labelled not recommended).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GrBhrzqWKgDg2LtStou9HU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqujO0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR4AQADy7xhh0zCPs3KKpxBYJ1Hm6\nXNEWMQ9BcrnhQplE6W+aIC9nuYYNMAKmxxQ880pGDlIhPXE9d3h4If3tBccGfdwH\nkcQ2Iz0wwAl49EBv02JZeJyOkTSZq/s5WRkIYc+yIbqAO8U2X0VU64oYTaQlEZrs\n/0xY3tevrokHiliBsG8KAu0ttSsoo594oUqFE7s2YjF2evvbpug4lpU93eAuW3pg\nwUglT8pc5OJYcaocGyRayw/FLeqwii0SgXfy/eesPjDFSv8nuGYW/FLVinBDMFLK\neyQlI35LNdpX1Q9uRcP5BGp0U8huJrFRXCGEByEAyro+sivpwK7abVq2O/tBkWl9\nN4/i5JAfDFJG67KmHqCYpWbCS+Jbd2cFOixAbJCluy62bSsId+aJwzik8NXEIUZ1\na/4P7wMfNgKu6g50qxxhp7rSF+W+JL3YiZwgC8wq/fVXHSjpuvyD3Jh/e4ZZQ5rK\nkmHxj46/NSyQhUnsovIT3KWAooO8TWOahlmnFKKyZNH/vmrIGPlnUkzgrhimSeg0\nuNyTw6Hw8Cs41/R7S9UwdnaOlQBBslUtPDbtRAWNvRLqbw1U6UrSNVYh4MlHLXSN\nfWfvDSod5HYkIRLTFszBV5QQLDc8El2J+FOrzYbv5C4YnTJKIVf7f7EjbEQGU7OU\n5m6zroh4dK8G2PpLKbir\n=cM8B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T09:30:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","