c7"}],"sha":"0f69fde7a0ec7046ee04e1e937efd97321099e04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/0f69fde7a0ec7046ee04e1e937efd97321099e04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47221942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/87ac4663f05f260e9203ef0541ff1dbfb5321fc7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T02:44:23Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T02:44:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Extract TaskRow component and enhance scheduled task UI (#1057)\n\n* feat(canvas): make the Scheduled list easier to scan and act on\n\n- Fixed-width cadence/last-run columns and a fixed Run now width so every\n  row lines up, including while a run is in progress.\n- Last run now shows state clearly: running spinner, red failure with the\n  error text, and a completed link that opens that run''s conversation.\n  Only the latest successful attempt is linked, never an older result.\n- Pause/Edit/Delete become icon buttons with tooltips; built-in tasks keep\n  an aligned slot for the missing delete action. Paused rows are dimmed.\n- Narrow layouts keep cadence and last run visible on a second line\n  instead of hiding failures.\n- Extract the row into TaskRow.tsx and record the result-link rule in the\n  scheduled-tasks knowledge doc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n* fix(harness): fail fast instead of hanging when launch prerequisites are stale\n\n`harness start` builds nothing, and with a stale workspace package or a\nmissing Electron SQLite binding the Electron main process wedges: CDP\naccepts the connection but never answers /json/list. getTargets'' fetch had\nno timeout, so waitFor sat on its first attempt and the 30s ready timeout\nnever fired (reproduced: >5 min hang, empty logs).\n\n- getTargets bounds each CDP HTTP request (2s), so a wedged launch now\n  fails at the ready timeout with a clear message and a harness:up hint.\n- start preflights the prerequisites it loads, reusing quickstart''s\n  buildTargets staleness, and fails in <0.1s pointing at harness:up.\n  --skip-preflight opts out; harness:up --skip-build passes it through.\n- --help leads with harness:up for first launch / cloud containers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n* fix(canvas): stop flagging the user''s own edits as agent edits\n\nThe SQLite change feed carries no writer, so every save the app makes\ncomes back as canvas:external-update. receiveExternal already recognised\nthe echo (revision <= baseline) and ignored it, but the transient\n\"agent edited\" ring was applied to every changed id regardless, so a\nplain drag flashed the purple ring on the node being moved.\n\nCanvasDocumentPersistence.foreignNodeIds now filters changed ids against\nthe states this client wrote: the acknowledged baseline, the payload of a\nsave still in flight (the event can beat its acknowledgement), and the\ndraft. Only nodes whose disk state matches none of them get the ring.\n\nVerified in the real app over SQLite: dragging a node no longer flags it\n(old code flagged it), and a canvas-cli title update still does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n* style(canvas): nested frames become outlined regions, not stacked surfaces\n\nNested frames alternated a gray wash and white by depth (6a780bc), and\nkept a hairline on top of the fill. A card inside a nested frame sat under\nfour layers of chrome (canvas, white root, gray region, card), each with\nits own fill, border and radius, and the gray wash was close enough to the\ncanvas that nested regions read as holes in the artboard.\n\nOnly the root frame is now a white surface. Nested frames at every depth\nare transparent regions bounded by a ~1 screen-pixel hairline; hover\ndarkens that hairline instead of adding the root''s 2px border inside it,\nand nested labels step down to 14px secondary text so depth is not carried\nby the outline alone. The even-depth class and --frame-nested-bg token are\ngone; --frame-nested-outline(-hover) replace them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2151228ce6e7831471cfac32adfff66461c629f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/b2151228ce6e7831471cfac32adfff66461c629f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/87ac4663f05f260e9203ef0541ff1dbfb5321fc7","verification":{"payload":"tree b2151228ce6e7831471cfac32adfff66461c629f\nparent 6a780bcef9ee096103659b9cb6bbba927d55d902\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790563463 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790563463 +0800\n\nExtract TaskRow component and enhance scheduled task UI (#1057)\n\n* feat(canvas): make the Scheduled list easier to scan and act on\n\n- Fixed-width cadence/last-run columns and a fixed Run now width so every\n  row lines up, including while a run is in progress.\n- Last run now shows state clearly: running spinner, red failure with the\n  error text, and a completed link that opens that run''s conversation.\n  Only the latest successful attempt is linked, never an older result.\n- Pause/Edit/Delete become icon buttons with tooltips; built-in tasks keep\n  an aligned slot for the missing delete action. Paused rows are dimmed.\n- Narrow layouts keep cadence and last run visible on a second line\n  instead of hiding failures.\n- Extract the row into TaskRow.tsx and record the result-link rule in the\n  scheduled-tasks knowledge doc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n* fix(harness): fail fast instead of hanging when launch prerequisites are stale\n\n`harness start` builds nothing, and with a stale workspace package or a\nmissing Electron SQLite binding the Electron main process wedges: CDP\naccepts the connection but never answers /json/list. getTargets'' fetch had\nno timeout, so waitFor sat on its first attempt and the 30s ready timeout\nnever fired (reproduced: >5 min hang, empty logs).\n\n- getTargets bounds each CDP HTTP request (2s), so a wedged launch now\n  fails at the ready timeout with a clear message and a harness:up hint.\n- start preflights the prerequisites it loads, reusing quickstart''s\n  buildTargets staleness, and fails in <0.1s pointing at harness:up.\n  --skip-preflight opts out; harness:up --skip-build passes it through.\n- --help leads with harness:up for first launch / cloud containers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n* fix(canvas): stop flagging the user''s own edits as agent edits\n\nThe SQLite change feed carries no writer, so every save the app makes\ncomes back as canvas:external-update. receiveExternal already recognised\nthe echo (revision <= baseline) and ignored it, but the transient\n\"agent edited\" ring was applied to every changed id regardless, so a\nplain drag flashed the purple ring on the node being moved.\n\nCanvasDocumentPersistence.foreignNodeIds now filters changed ids against\nthe states this client wrote: the acknowledged baseline, the payload of a\nsave still in flight (the event can beat its acknowledgement), and the\ndraft. Only nodes whose disk state matches none of them get the ring.\n\nVerified in the real app over SQLite: dragging a node no longer flags it\n(old code flagged it), and a canvas-cli title update still does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n* style(canvas): nested frames become outlined regions, not stacked surfaces\n\nNested frames alternated a gray wash and white by depth (6a780bc), and\nkept a hairline on top of the fill. A card inside a nested frame sat under\nfour layers of chrome (canvas, white root, gray region, card), each with\nits own fill, border and radius, and the gray wash was close enough to the\ncanvas that nested regions read as holes in the artboard.\n\nOnly the root frame is now a white surface. Nested frames at every depth\nare transparent regions bounded by a ~1 screen-pixel hairline; hover\ndarkens that hairline instead of adding the root''s 2px border inside it,\nand nested labels step down to 14px secondary text so depth is not carried\nby the outline alone. The even-depth class and --frame-nested-bg token are\ngone; --frame-nested-outline(-hover) replace them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BN1MibNiVJsQVQnoRd4KVB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",