p+DaLvFfbI4yNHLI7NVafb3onnkz1XwMgf8lzy8\njx01vxamzAanOaO+WbG1\n=ehly\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T10:48:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/11741077d074e616333a059d1b87080a5b98b38e","node_id":"C_kwDORBlpqtoAKDExNzQxMDc3ZDA3NGU2MTYzMzNhMDU5ZDFiODcwODBhNWI5OGIzOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08","sha":"668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08"}],"sha":"11741077d074e616333a059d1b87080a5b98b38e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/11741077d074e616333a059d1b87080a5b98b38e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47221942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:09:33Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:09:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add harness:up quickstart and dev mode for canvas-workspace (#1037)\n\n* feat(canvas): make the real-app harness work in cloud/proxy containers\n\nReal-Electron debugging failed in egress-proxied Linux sandboxes at two\npoints:\n\n- `pnpm install` aborted: the postinstall `electron-rebuild` needs Electron\n  headers from electronjs.org, which proxies commonly deny. The new\n  `scripts/setup/rebuild-native.mjs` falls back to a node-gyp build against\n  host Node headers; node-pty 1.x is N-API, so that binary loads in Electron.\n- Every HTTPS webview failed with net_error -202: Chromium on Linux ignores\n  NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS and trusts only $HOME/.pki/nssdb. The harness driver\n  gains `--ca-cert <pem>` (or PULSE_CANVAS_HARNESS_CA_CERT) to import CAs into\n  the profile HOME''s NSS db; profile=real is refused.\n\nAlso documents the mock-LLM chat launch, lists --headless in the CLI help,\nand corrects the README claim that headless sets ELECTRON_DISABLE_SANDBOX\n(the driver passes --no-sandbox).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* feat(canvas): one-command real-app debugging with harness:up\n\n`pnpm --filter canvas-workspace harness:up` takes a fresh container to a\nrunning, driveable Electron app without manual steps (~100s cold, ~4s warm);\n`harness:down` closes the session and stops the mock LLM.\n\nquickstart.mjs (Node builtins only, so it runs before pnpm install) skips\nevery satisfied step: apt-installs Xvfb/certutil when root on display-less\nLinux, installs dependencies when node_modules, Electron, or node-pty are\nmissing, rebuilds engine -> agent-teams -> canvas-cli -> app from the first\nstale output, starts harness/mock-llm.mjs unless a model key is set, and\nlaunches with --headless and --ca-cert chosen for the host.\n\nCA import now uses content-hashed nicknames and skips certificates already\nin the NSS db, so warm relaunches on the demo HOME stay fast. The\ncanvas-harness skill makes harness:up its default entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* feat(canvas): default harness:up to electron-vite dev with HMR\n\nThe debug loop was bounded by the ~67s production app build on every code\nchange. `harness start --dev` now runs `electron-vite dev --watch` behind the\nsame CDP session, and `harness:up` uses it by default (`--built` keeps the\nproduction bundle for perf/packaging checks). Measured in a cloud container:\nusable UI in ~16s instead of ~70s, renderer edits hot-update in ~2s without\na page reload, and main/preload edits restart Electron in ~12s on the same\nCDP port.\n\n- Dev sessions record processGroup so close signals electron-vite, its\n  Electron child and the dev server together.\n- Dev writes dev bundles into dist/main and dist/preload; quickstart marks\n  that and forces an app rebuild on the next --built launch.\n- start now waits for React to replace the boot splash. The previous\n  absence-only check passed on the initial about:blank, so a screenshot\n  right after start could capture the splash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* fix(canvas): harness start waits for settled content; resolve user paths from invocation dir\n\n- A screenshot taken right after `harness:up` showed empty node bodies and a\n  blank webview: start returned once the React shell rendered, before lazy\n  node bodies, file previews and webview guests finished. New readiness.mjs\n  then waits for an explicit list of first-paint signals (.node-body:empty,\n  .file-preview--loading, .chat-messages--loading, webview isLoading) to be\n  clear on consecutive polls. It is best effort: after 15s it warns with what\n  is pending instead of failing, and deliberately avoids a generic --loading\n  match that states like a blocked update check would hold forever.\n- `pnpm --filter canvas-workspace harness screenshot --output x.png` wrote to\n  apps/canvas-workspace/apps/... because pnpm runs scripts from the package\n  dir. --output and --ca-cert now resolve against INIT_CWD, the directory\n  pnpm was invoked from.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* fix(canvas): treat tsup.config.ts as a harness:up build input\n\nA package''s tsup.config.ts owns its entry list, so an entry added there\nalone (as storage''s local-workspace-files was, alongside src) must mark the\npackage stale. harness:up previously compared only src/ and package.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* fix(canvas): address harness:up review findings\n\nFrom the Codex review on #1037, each reproduced before fixing:\n- Worktree isolation: dependencies install through `pnpm bootstrap:worktree`,\n  and quickstart runs its assertLocalNodeModules guard before trusting an\n  existing node_modules (root AGENTS rule for linked worktrees).\n- Electron system libraries: an `ldd` preflight finds missing libraries; as\n  root it installs Playwright''s Chromium dependency set, then falls back to\n  apt''s fix-broken repair when apt refuses that transaction over unmet\n  dependencies. Otherwise it fails with the missing names instead of an\n  Electron loader crash before CDP. Reproduced by removing libatk.\n- Windows dev sessions: stopProcess kills the tree with `taskkill /T` since\n  process.kill cannot take a negative process-group pid there.\n- `--force` relaunch now cleans the replaced session''s disposable HOME\n  (temp, or clone''s copy of real data), alive or not.\n- harness:down signals the mock LLM only if its pid still runs\n  mock-llm.mjs (a stale state file''s pid may be reused), and waits for it\n  to exit so an immediate harness:up cannot reuse a dying mock.\n- canvas-cli''s skills/ is a build input, since its build copies skills into\n  the dist that unpackaged Canvas tooling reads.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"25753ce241b72ab19e53cc6e17d5194b5212b0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/25753ce241b72ab19e53cc6e17d5194b5212b0e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08","verification":{"payload":"tree 25753ce241b72ab19e53cc6e17d5194b5212b0e4\nparent 587b9255e344fd66622feca45a988d4d069a96b2\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790417373 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790417373 +0800\n\nAdd harness:up quickstart and dev mode for canvas-workspace (#1037)\n\n* feat(canvas): make the real-app harness work in cloud/proxy containers\n\nReal-Electron debugging failed in egress-proxied Linux sandboxes at two\npoints:\n\n- `pnpm install` aborted: the postinstall `electron-rebuild` needs Electron\n  headers from electronjs.org, which proxies commonly deny. The new\n  `scripts/setup/rebuild-native.mjs` falls back to a node-gyp build against\n  host Node headers; node-pty 1.x is N-API, so that binary loads in Electron.\n- Every HTTPS webview failed with net_error -202: Chromium on Linux ignores\n  NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS and trusts only $HOME/.pki/nssdb. The harness driver\n  gains `--ca-cert <pem>` (or PULSE_CANVAS_HARNESS_CA_CERT) to import CAs into\n  the profile HOME''s NSS db; profile=real is refused.\n\nAlso documents the mock-LLM chat launch, lists --headless in the CLI help,\nand corrects the README claim that headless sets ELECTRON_DISABLE_SANDBOX\n(the driver passes --no-sandbox).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* feat(canvas): one-command real-app debugging with harness:up\n\n`pnpm --filter canvas-workspace harness:up` takes a fresh container to a\nrunning, driveable Electron app without manual steps (~100s cold, ~4s warm);\n`harness:down` closes the session and stops the mock LLM.\n\nquickstart.mjs (Node builtins only, so it runs before pnpm install) skips\nevery satisfied step: apt-installs Xvfb/certutil when root on display-less\nLinux, installs dependencies when node_modules, Electron, or node-pty are\nmissing, rebuilds engine -> agent-teams -> canvas-cli -> app from the first\nstale output, starts harness/mock-llm.mjs unless a model key is set, and\nlaunches with --headless and --ca-cert chosen for the host.\n\nCA import now uses content-hashed nicknames and skips certificates already\nin the NSS db, so warm relaunches on the demo HOME stay fast. The\ncanvas-harness skill makes harness:up its default entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* feat(canvas): default harness:up to electron-vite dev with HMR\n\nThe debug loop was bounded by the ~67s production app build on every code\nchange. `harness start --dev` now runs `electron-vite dev --watch` behind the\nsame CDP session, and `harness:up` uses it by default (`--built` keeps the\nproduction bundle for perf/packaging checks). Measured in a cloud container:\nusable UI in ~16s instead of ~70s, renderer edits hot-update in ~2s without\na page reload, and main/preload edits restart Electron in ~12s on the same\nCDP port.\n\n- Dev sessions record processGroup so close signals electron-vite, its\n  Electron child and the dev server together.\n- Dev writes dev bundles into dist/main and dist/preload; quickstart marks\n  that and forces an app rebuild on the next --built launch.\n- start now waits for React to replace the boot splash. The previous\n  absence-only check passed on the initial about:blank, so a screenshot\n  right after start could capture the splash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* fix(canvas): harness start waits for settled content; resolve user paths from invocation dir\n\n- A screenshot taken right after `harness:up` showed empty node bodies and a\n  blank webview: start returned once the React shell rendered, before lazy\n  node bodies, file previews and webview guests finished. New readiness.mjs\n  then waits for an explicit list of first-paint signals (.node-body:empty,\n  .file-preview--loading, .chat-messages--loading, webview isLoading) to be\n  clear on consecutive polls. It is best effort: after 15s it warns with what\n  is pending instead of failing, and deliberately avoids a generic --loading\n  match that states like a blocked update check would hold forever.\n- `pnpm --filter canvas-workspace harness screenshot --output x.png` wrote to\n  apps/canvas-workspace/apps/... because pnpm runs scripts from the package\n  dir. --output and --ca-cert now resolve against INIT_CWD, the directory\n  pnpm was invoked from.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* fix(canvas): treat tsup.config.ts as a harness:up build input\n\nA package''s tsup.config.ts owns its entry list, so an entry added there\nalone (as storage''s local-workspace-files was, alongside src) must mark the\npackage stale. harness:up previously compared only src/ and package.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n* fix(canvas): address harness:up review findings\n\nFrom the Codex review on #1037, each reproduced before fixing:\n- Worktree isolation: dependencies install through `pnpm bootstrap:worktree`,\n  and quickstart runs its assertLocalNodeModules guard before trusting an\n  existing node_modules (root AGENTS rule for linked worktrees).\n- Electron system libraries: an `ldd` preflight finds missing libraries; as\n  root it installs Playwright''s Chromium dependency set, then falls back to\n  apt''s fix-broken repair when apt refuses that transaction over unmet\n  dependencies. Otherwise it fails with the missing names instead of an\n  Electron loader crash before CDP. Reproduced by removing libatk.\n- Windows dev sessions: stopProcess kills the tree with `taskkill /T` since\n  process.kill cannot take a negative process-group pid there.\n- `--force` relaunch now cleans the replaced session''s disposable HOME\n  (temp, or clone''s copy of real data), alive or not.\n- harness:down signals the mock LLM only if its pid still runs\n  mock-llm.mjs (a stale state file''s pid may be reused), and waits for it\n  to exit so an immediate harness:up cannot reuse a dying mock.\n- canvas-cli''s skills/ is a build input, since its build copies skills into\n  the dist that unpackaged Canvas tooling reads.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXMEucLGwTyUG1KEXc3bwK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt5ndCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqQsQAAVtwHbQ//mdMDZghniiaNSD\noGIC+9naVQyEFdJkyGppGxPlir9FAwoRIdSOOeenI16OG6U2es+IIEG4DmAUnr0q\nkNo/FO21AV2MYQKQLnyTHA1ORETo9wmHGyhO9FAlViwK8lYJx29lat319lIg4/oo\nY9lPVsiomtwn9IeqqqvnqFe/B/YaZsb2d0QycErlT6PxvoUQTo3usxmoG8J0zp7C\nGrGsMm6124vvfI0ytvmTU+Q9RQ5jRkkCEnXvFjHLDJB5alTdNJ6CvcY9vXS8lvan\nqs30zbNGPOWBYK+71L/sozYORe6+5aW5C5I3PT6buRb6E1vmXdI58KX8TJxG6S3I\nK7d/1d6ywCoVGjW9ATCLM3WOuOKIXIfWE6m0SdtnNpLsoX5wtgTCms3A8Y4Wzcy/\nX6YV+cvPvFwq+XbmmQNM3YgYbh9tE5zAbR/AnwEP45w+FVirlOmcB5VFfGj387y/\n7FABMuW/LzgYMcZ8DQPddQUQCH8Ut7dIFLTV2QOp1FMgQFN/OI+lA9DF/9p4zEzT\nGmaXyX6oUGdRWBdGUCg8Cbrz6uxuv/HWP2pPKQ/ptb7tAJUxbFjMgQvPDcK+i1NZ\njwCZAy1CAn9VElWmiqbAZQmwZThZUj9WnLag+V50i78D46lN2vg8ubT3dUFIs4MF\n1EETvAkccPX8S1+V/hqK\n=YHgR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T10:09:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08","node_id":"C_kwDORBlpqtoAKDY2ODA5N2IwNTk5MDlhZDA4NTVkM2Y4OTE2MzU3OGM1YzAzMTNkMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/587b9255e344fd66622feca45a988d4d069a96b2","sha":"587b9255e344fd66622feca45a988d4d069a96b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/587b9255e344fd66622feca45a988d4d069a96b2"}],"sha":"668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/668097b059909ad0855d3f89163578c5c0313d08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47221942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/587b9255e344fd66622feca45a988d4d069a96b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:47:36Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:47:36Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"message":"fix(canvas): restore end-to-end conversation timing traces\n\nCorrelate renderer submissions and runtime phases by run ID, include durable completion and UI milestones, and add local timing JSON export. Serialize trace storage reads and writes and cover the timing boundaries with regression tests.","tree":{"sha":"b31cde8e8868abf43e7d48dd528a28adae80a52a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/b31cde8e8868abf43e7d48dd528a28adae80a52a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/587b9255e344fd66622feca45a988d4d069a96b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47221942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/587b9255e344fd66622feca45a988d4d069a96b2","node_id":"C_kwDORBlpqtoAKDU4N2I5MjU1ZTM0NGZkNjY2MjJmZWNhNDVhOTg4ZDRkMDY5YTk2YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/ca1b2ef346da221b1f0dd7fec813b6ed501eba8f","sha":"ca1b2ef346da221b1f0dd7fec813b6ed501eba8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pu