a1b2ef346da221b1f0dd7fec813b6ed501eba8f","node_id":"C_kwDORBlpqtoAKGNhMWIyZWYzNDZkYTIyMWIxZjBkZDdmZWM4MTNiNmVkNTAxZWJhOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a","sha":"bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a"}],"sha":"ca1b2ef346da221b1f0dd7fec813b6ed501eba8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/ca1b2ef346da221b1f0dd7fec813b6ed501eba8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47221942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T02:41:13Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T02:41:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(storage): WorkspaceFiles (S3), and stop terminal output from committing the whole canvas (#1050)\n\n* feat(storage): route Canvas Markdown and attachments through WorkspaceFiles (S3)\n\nAdds a WorkspaceFiles repository to @pulse-coder/storage: text and byte\nreads with a content version, compare-and-swap or create-only writes,\nconditional removal, directory watching, and an explicit localPath escape\nhatch. The local adapter ports the editor save semantics (symlinked files\nedited in place, mode kept, atomic same-directory replace, per-file write\nlane). Versions are sha256:<hex> of the bytes, the scheme file write\nintents already use; sameFileVersion accepts the bare digests earlier\nreleases stored in fileSource.version, so upgrades do not rewrite notes.\n\nCanvas main now reaches Markdown and attachment content through it:\n- note editor and dock preview read/save, and the Markdown index reads\n  and directory watcher;\n- note creation and content writes from file:createNote,\n  canvas_create_node, node updates and the runtime MCP server, plus\n  agent context reads (notes and the workspace AGENTS.md text);\n- attachments: image save (create-only), delete, dimension reads, and\n  export reads.\n\nReal-path consumers (terminal-agent prompt files, save-dialog exports,\nimport staging, legacy migration) stay direct by design.\nfiles/workspace-files.test.ts keeps the content-owning modules free of\ndirect fs content I/O. The spec marks S3 delivered and records the\ndecisions in history/2026-09-25-s3-file-repository.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(storage): unlink symlinked entries and accept Windows UNC file URIs\n\nCodex review follow-ups for WorkspaceFiles:\n- remove() unlinks the addressed entry. A symlinked img-* attachment\n  deleted its link target, which could live outside the workspace;\n  deleteSavedImage only validates the lexical path.\n- On Windows, a file URI host names a UNC share (\\\\server\\share\\...).\n  Rejecting every host broke note and attachment access on network\n  shares; other platforms still reject remote hosts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): stop saving Coding Agent output on the canvas\n\nEvery running Coding Agent serialized its terminal buffer into node data\nevery two seconds, so any output committed the whole canvas: ~1 save and 1\nfull reload per 2s, ~7 MB/min of WAL writes with 8 agents, and a workspace\nrevision that moved constantly, making concurrent `pulse-canvas` writes fail\nwith revision_conflict.\n\nThe CLI resumes its own conversation, so the saved text was redundant.\nCoding Agent nodes now persist only a changed CWD. The owner terminal hands\nxterm''s rendered text to main (`pty:snapshot`), kept in memory by\n`terminal/session-output.ts` (preferred over the raw redraw stream, bounded,\nretained after exit). Node detail, dock_read_tab, and the Agent Team detail\npanel (`pty:getScrollback`) read it from there. Output saved by earlier\nreleases is dropped on the next launch. Plain terminal nodes are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): save terminal node output once a minute, on exit, and before quit\n\nTerminal nodes still saved their buffer into the canvas every two seconds,\nwith the same whole-canvas commits and revision churn the Coding Agent fix\nremoved. They have no conversation to resume, so the saved copy stays, but it\nis now written at most once a minute, on process exit, on unmount, and when\nthe window goes away. Every tick in between only publishes to main, and\nnode reads (context builder, runtime MCP server) prefer main''s live text.\n\nUnload and quit needed their own paths:\n- Closing a window: beforeunload listeners run in registration order, so a\n  node written there could miss the canvas''s own flush. The canvas now\n  flushes again on pagehide, which follows every beforeunload listener.\n- Quitting: before-quit closed storage before windows closed, so a\n  renderer''s unload save reached a closed store (also true for any canvas\n  edit still in its 800ms debounce). Main now asks each window to save\n  first (canvas:flush-before-quit / canvas:flushed, 1.5s timeout); the\n  renderer lets node bodies write, then flushes every registered workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* perf(canvas): keep output-store IPC and quit flush out of the gated bundles\n\nThe perf job failed its entry-chunk gzip and main-bundle raw gates: master\nsits within 1 KB of both limits, and this PR added 0.05 KB and 0.84 KB.\n\n- Main: the `pty:snapshot` / `pty:getScrollback` handlers move to\n  `terminal/scrollback-ipc.ts`, loaded with bootstrap''s other lazy IPC, and\n  the quit handshake module loads on quit.\n- Renderer: the quit handshake and the window-close flush now live in the\n  terminal node runtime, which is already a lazy chunk, instead of the\n  canvas document code in the entry chunk. The canvas `pagehide` flush is\n  gone: the terminal''s beforeunload listener writes the node and flushes\n  every workspace itself. `workspacePersistence` only exposes its registry.\n\nMeasured locally: entry gzip 213.50 KB -> 213.495 KB (limit 213 rounded),\nmain raw 720.69 KB -> 720.42 KB (limit 720 rounded); master is 213.48 /\n719.85. Reload and quit saves re-verified in the built app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): address review on live terminal output\n\n- Read-only agent previews (dock canvas preview, reference drawer) read\n  main''s live output on mount, falling back to the saved copy; they\n  showed \"no saved agent output\" once agent output stopped being saved.\n- Terminal nodes publish their final lines to main on exit and on unmount,\n  so main''s retained snapshot is not stuck at the last two-second tick.\n- Each publish tick also refreshes the shell''s CWD; unload and quit saves\n  use it instead of the value from the last once-a-minute canvas save.\n- The quit handshake now runs tasks registered by terminal nodes, each\n  flushing its own workspace through the existing\n  flushWorkspacePersistence. workspacePersistence.ts is back to master, so\n  nothing new lands in the entry chunk (213.47 KB gzip vs 213.48 on master).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fcbd6a7bfc7b37f4556189ae2d08658c7580e9b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/fcbd6a7bfc7b37f4556189ae2d08658c7580e9b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a","verification":{"payload":"tree fcbd6a7bfc7b37f4556189ae2d08658c7580e9b8\nparent b4d0c6e6d69ae4496d7f165a16b72df510b7b0fe\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790390473 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790390473 +0800\n\nfeat(storage): WorkspaceFiles (S3), and stop terminal output from committing the whole canvas (#1050)\n\n* feat(storage): route Canvas Markdown and attachments through WorkspaceFiles (S3)\n\nAdds a WorkspaceFiles repository to @pulse-coder/storage: text and byte\nreads with a content version, compare-and-swap or create-only writes,\nconditional removal, directory watching, and an explicit localPath escape\nhatch. The local adapter ports the editor save semantics (symlinked files\nedited in place, mode kept, atomic same-directory replace, per-file write\nlane). Versions are sha256:<hex> of the bytes, the scheme file write\nintents already use; sameFileVersion accepts the bare digests earlier\nreleases stored in fileSource.version, so upgrades do not rewrite notes.\n\nCanvas main now reaches Markdown and attachment content through it:\n- note editor and dock preview read/save, and the Markdown index reads\n  and directory watcher;\n- note creation and content writes from file:createNote,\n  canvas_create_node, node updates and the runtime MCP server, plus\n  agent context reads (notes and the workspace AGENTS.md text);\n- attachments: image save (create-only), delete, dimension reads, and\n  export reads.\n\nReal-path consumers (terminal-agent prompt files, save-dialog exports,\nimport staging, legacy migration) stay direct by design.\nfiles/workspace-files.test.ts keeps the content-owning modules free of\ndirect fs content I/O. The spec marks S3 delivered and records the\ndecisions in history/2026-09-25-s3-file-repository.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(storage): unlink symlinked entries and accept Windows UNC file URIs\n\nCodex review follow-ups for WorkspaceFiles:\n- remove() unlinks the addressed entry. A symlinked img-* attachment\n  deleted its link target, which could live outside the workspace;\n  deleteSavedImage only validates the lexical path.\n- On Windows, a file URI host names a UNC share (\\\\server\\share\\...).\n  Rejecting every host broke note and attachment access on network\n  shares; other platforms still reject remote hosts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): stop saving Coding Agent output on the canvas\n\nEvery running Coding Agent serialized its terminal buffer into node data\nevery two seconds, so any output committed the whole canvas: ~1 save and 1\nfull reload per 2s, ~7 MB/min of WAL writes with 8 agents, and a workspace\nrevision that moved constantly, making concurrent `pulse-canvas` writes fail\nwith revision_conflict.\n\nThe CLI resumes its own conversation, so the saved text was redundant.\nCoding Agent nodes now persist only a changed CWD. The owner terminal hands\nxterm''s rendered text to main (`pty:snapshot`), kept in memory by\n`terminal/session-output.ts` (preferred over the raw redraw stream, bounded,\nretained after exit). Node detail, dock_read_tab, and the Agent Team detail\npanel (`pty:getScrollback`) read it from there. Output saved by earlier\nreleases is dropped on the next launch. Plain terminal nodes are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): save terminal node output once a minute, on exit, and before quit\n\nTerminal nodes still saved their buffer into the canvas every two seconds,\nwith the same whole-canvas commits and revision churn the Coding Agent fix\nremoved. They have no conversation to resume, so the saved copy stays, but it\nis now written at most once a minute, on process exit, on unmount, and when\nthe window goes away. Every tick in between only publishes to main, and\nnode reads (context builder, runtime MCP server) prefer main''s live text.\n\nUnload and quit needed their own paths:\n- Closing a window: beforeunload listeners run in registration order, so a\n  node written there could miss the canvas''s own flush. The canvas now\n  flushes again on pagehide, which follows every beforeunload listener.\n- Quitting: before-quit closed storage before windows closed, so a\n  renderer''s unload save reached a closed store (also true for any canvas\n  edit still in its 800ms debounce). Main now asks each window to save\n  first (canvas:flush-before-quit / canvas:flushed, 1.5s timeout); the\n  renderer lets node bodies write, then flushes every registered workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* perf(canvas): keep output-store IPC and quit flush out of the gated bundles\n\nThe perf job failed its entry-chunk gzip and main-bundle raw gates: master\nsits within 1 KB of both limits, and this PR added 0.05 KB and 0.84 KB.\n\n- Main: the `pty:snapshot` / `pty:getScrollback` handlers move to\n  `terminal/scrollback-ipc.ts`, loaded with bootstrap''s other lazy IPC, and\n  the quit handshake module loads on quit.\n- Renderer: the quit handshake and the window-close flush now live in the\n  terminal node runtime, which is already a lazy chunk, instead of the\n  canvas document code in the entry chunk. The canvas `pagehide` flush is\n  gone: the terminal''s beforeunload listener writes the node and flushes\n  every workspace itself. `workspacePersistence` only exposes its registry.\n\nMeasured locally: entry gzip 213.50 KB -> 213.495 KB (limit 213 rounded),\nmain raw 720.69 KB -> 720.42 KB (limit 720 rounded); master is 213.48 /\n719.85. Reload and quit saves re-verified in the built app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): address review on live terminal output\n\n- Read-only agent previews (dock canvas preview, reference drawer) read\n  main''s live output on mount, falling back to the saved copy; they\n  showed \"no saved agent output\" once agent output stopped being saved.\n- Terminal nodes publish their final lines to main on exit and on unmount,\n  so main''s retained snapshot is not stuck at the last two-second tick.\n- Each publish tick also refreshes the shell''s CWD; unload and quit saves\n  use it instead of the value from the last once-a-minute canvas save.\n- The quit handshake now runs tasks registered by terminal nodes, each\n  flushing its own workspace through the existing\n  flushWorkspacePersistence. workspacePersistence.ts is back to master, so\n  nothing new lands in the entry chunk (213.47 KB gzip vs 213.48 on master).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtzDJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjdcQAAT2U5h3Zxh4jZq/sqDtcDyV\nCWotF9ZR+ExTxyeoShZWLd/mN5E0o3ujGOOl6QLIII7thVydK8kXtU3HCu9ShZ+F\nVYEqkrAnfflXFivyd5NP82cY4C7OEIiGbJ4PskyKuQKF/t6nwnHp0l9vFIoVW8qq\nT/DN0xB8tfcvztq4qVySiqkvAJ9x6BN53U0LiA29ZupKPSml4vjX49Lx6LologVk\nOptciK2tGy0iOLrNg3N6oneEbtoJuYbOjogpvnq7XuEG6oxyto+XfQdfHyTgWVvD\nB9eNyxSK/KT0aERe68mM1HT27GJbbBJ9S+RCuoQ8ZgJpc5r0foQauWIi7EKUM7nO\n+FS0/3sp4y8TX2aVrDhKiGToMsaboUMdQQ731McnmhWWcOY2zB4MZ9j4uQsjgGRR\ngNhVgQMs/vNfHleN4NBnT/IVZhYUuuxeFconSXsShDVOS6br3PBXHMFDp9GtgW3+\nWO2AzXfz1MLqZdJdvb+xaWt2j1P15SB2pe4qy0j4w07XIZjcnOejFdX73lY1hMIV\nWozzVl16DN3/Lm2BwuQrL13lJCcTnSIBS8CYiiC/XRuc0dgIHlU1c1YQ+452rFWk\nBkUWcV6ZN0Vrw3QjvjUqpAIxQALSzm0Otwu+Hwaudo6p97h2gqznzZlFBPAkztZF\n1bOCcUt04PwuU8hXdfaN\n=2oHs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T02:41:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a","node_id":"C_kwDORBlpqtoAKGJmYTgwNjZjMWRjNWE3NmJlZmUxOTFhMjBkNWYyMWNiMzU2ODYwMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commit/b4d0c6e6d69ae4496d7f165a16b72df510b7b0fe","sha":"b4d0c6e6d69ae4496d7f165a16b72df510b7b0fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/b4d0c6e6d69ae4496d7f165a16b72df510b7b0fe"}],"sha":"bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/bfa8066c1dc5a76befe191a20d5f21cb3568602a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47221942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hua-bang","id":47221942,"login":"hua-bang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjIxOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hua-bang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/commits/b4d0c6e6d69ae4496d7f165a16b72df510b7b0fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T12:27:45Z","email":"huabang001124@gmail.com","name":"Jasper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T12:27:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve Canvas and CLI usability issues (#1049)\n\n* feat(canvas): unify chat session actions and add reply branching\n\n* fix(canvas): simplify chat activity copy within bundle budget\n\n* fix: address plugin labels, session status, host eval and startup noise\n\nShow installed plugin names and preserve background session running indicators. Reconcile in-flight polls without reviving completed runs or hiding new remote runs.\n\nKeep host renderer evaluation on the live Canvas workspace without implicit navigation, and consolidate CLI startup diagnostics across Ink and readline.\n\nAdd regression coverage for issues #1045, #1046, #1047 and #1048.","tree":{"sha":"6dd0b8f8d19a0ed71a8401bcc75eb0b2d6f86bf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/6dd0b8f8d19a0ed71a8401bcc75eb0b2d6f86bf2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/b4d0c6e6d69ae4496d7f165a16b72df510b7b0fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 6dd0b8f8d19a0ed71a8401bcc75eb0b2d6f86bf2\nparent 724bd6c0fcfde73967c73f990eaf4db5e8d76c26\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790339265 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790339265 +0800\n\nfix: resolve Canvas and CLI usability issues (#1049)\n\n* feat(canvas): unify chat session actions and add reply branching\n\n* fix(canvas): simplify chat activity copy within bundle budget\n\n* fix: address plugin labels, session status, host eval and startup noise\n\nShow installed plugin names and preserve background session running indicators. Reconcile in-flight polls without reviving completed runs or hiding new remote runs.\n\nKeep host renderer evaluation on the live Canvas workspace without implicit navigation, and consolidate CLI startup diagnostics across Ink and readline.\n\nAdd regression coverage for issues #1045, #1046, #1047 and #1048.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtmjBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ68QAAsG903GTqh8hJttSzREMCk6\nl4wBfDrsQ3+VJVRftIViBystwsZz6JdEePOrwFr1o4aQIUBgCbk0uUz5vo4Pydih\nll33ewJOESYvo6jS6RRR1GIBMgqBHJZrlB7CiXpO6xxNyuhGJuiKjHUrmds3ouEU\npjaW1NGSeAWL+rzW4udl0dkDnxNZCHwtQv1yeEoi2ZCA+40PJ+IJo