3 (file repository) until Markdown access is reworked or sync starts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): make chat Stop, Enter queue, and edit/regenerate work\n\n- Enter during a running turn queues the draft like the Queue button,\n  behind the same session-loading veto.\n- Manual Stop uses abortAndClearQueue on both chat surfaces, so a queued\n  follow-up no longer starts right after the stop.\n- Edit and regenerate resend the user turn in the same conversation:\n  the renderer passes truncateAt and ConversationRuntime cuts its history\n  at that user message under the turn lease. Regenerate maps the clicked\n  assistant message to the user turn it answered and keeps attachments.\n  A stale index fails the turn instead of cutting unrelated history.\n\nVerified in the built Electron app against a local streaming model:\nEnter queue, Stop clearing the queue, regenerate after stop and after a\ncompleted reply, edit, and history after restart. Removes the three\nresolved known-defect entries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* perf(canvas): stop re-rendering the whole chat history on each keystroke\n\nEvery message in a thread is mounted, and ChatMessage was not memoized.\nIts callbacks also changed identity on every render, so each composer\nkeystroke and stream delta re-rendered all messages. At 800 turns\n(~12,000 DOM elements) a keystroke took 72 ms p50 / 210 ms max to paint.\n\nChatMessage is now memoized, and ChatMessages passes identity-stable\nforwarders (useStableRowHandlers) that call the latest surface handler.\nonToggleSection takes the row index, so the list no longer creates an\ninline closure per row.\n\nMeasured in the built Electron app with an 800-turn conversation:\nkeystroke latency 72/210 ms -> 18/27 ms (p50/max); long tasks while\nstreaming a reply 680 ms -> 78 ms. Pre-merge build 0a4c2c5 measured the\nsame as before this change, so the lag predates the storage migration.\nOpening a long thread (~4.7 s) is unchanged and needs virtualization.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae2a77a085371efdf6a8b64566ea2b52bc6496cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/trees/ae2a77a085371efdf6a8b64566ea2b52bc6496cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hua-bang/pulse-agent/git/commits/71f1e7f5f4ee02bc461ae517ceb43dc47364cf14","verification":{"payload":"tree ae2a77a085371efdf6a8b64566ea2b52bc6496cb\nparent d20c3fd017e799ec3d11157ff61f3f444f276984\nauthor Jasper <huabang001124@gmail.com> 1790272315 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790272315 +0800\n\nfix(canvas): chat Stop/Enter queue/edit/regenerate, and long-thread typing lag (#1039)\n\n* docs(harness): mark unified-storage S1/S2 merged and S3 shelved\n\nPR #1035 merged S1 and S2. Record that, and record the decision to shelve\nS3 (file repository) until Markdown access is reworked or sync starts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* fix(canvas): make chat Stop, Enter queue, and edit/regenerate work\n\n- Enter during a running turn queues the draft like the Queue button,\n  behind the same session-loading veto.\n- Manual Stop uses abortAndClearQueue on both chat surfaces, so a queued\n  follow-up no longer starts right after the stop.\n- Edit and regenerate resend the user turn in the same conversation:\n  the renderer passes truncateAt and ConversationRuntime cuts its history\n  at that user message under the turn lease. Regenerate maps the clicked\n  assistant message to the user turn it answered and keeps attachments.\n  A stale index fails the turn instead of cutting unrelated history.\n\nVerified in the built Electron app against a local streaming model:\nEnter queue, Stop clearing the queue, regenerate after stop and after a\ncompleted reply, edit, and history after restart. Removes the three\nresolved known-defect entries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n* perf(canvas): stop re-rendering the whole chat history on each keystroke\n\nEvery message in a thread is mounted, and ChatMessage was not memoized.\nIts callbacks also changed identity on every render, so each composer\nkeystroke and stream delta re-rendered all messages. At 800 turns\n(~12,000 DOM elements) a keystroke took 72 ms p50 / 210 ms max to paint.\n\nChatMessage is now memoized, and ChatMessages passes identity-stable\nforwarders (useStableRowHandlers) that call the latest surface handler.\nonToggleSection takes the row index, so the list no longer creates an\ninline closure per row.\n\nMeasured in the built Electron app with an 800-turn conversation:\nkeystroke latency 72/210 ms -> 18/27 ms (p50/max); long tasks while\nstreaming a reply 680 ms -> 78 ms. Pre-merge build 0a4c2c5 measured the\nsame as before this change, so the lag predates the storage migration.\nOpening a long thread (~4.7 s) is unchanged and needs virtualization.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ssc1wCNTgSjRPjz2uMiz5d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtWM7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYqgQACx+7o9Z5X9fvqwAtRHFd0Zh\ndCkUL8dhMgw4alOK0eBs+4f9vIm9dgmpRaWagsMx8qVvHP8NPnXmCH6pHyBpk84o\nfThj89E6H8Ug8EWp7QPuT4QoFAbnbRddJ6U/h806GUsU99OWQItOa0PcMH/+zxq6\nQVaFbAq92t3s2xZsg7DUs0/DKtronvTqeHCEKLKItzj4mMv4EDbGcro+ev93jjK3\nH9ub3aYP3Zf/p80IBGXL0HAF6D/sTj926Bl1F6KoHFP2653N+++wYkMdgnfALLKh\n1kkSKQX/ibHFBCdZRlSorFoJvwBxiX5zt6n0+